# Cloudflare Pages redirects — one live URL per page.
#
# Why this file exists. Cloudflare Pages serves an HTML page at its
# extension-less path (/menu serves menu.html) and then 308-redirects the
# .html path back to it. So every page had two live URLs, while the page's
# own <link rel="canonical"> and its sitemap.xml entry named the .html one
# — the declared canonical URL was itself a redirect.
#
# These rules settle it the way the site already declares. Two rules per
# page are needed:
#
#   * the .html path is served directly with a 200, so the canonical URL,
#     the sitemap entry and every internal link resolve with no redirect
#     hop;
#   * the extension-less path 301s to the .html path, so the duplicate URL
#     is retired permanently instead of being served a second time.
#
# A 301 on its own would not do: Pages' built-in .html -> extension-less
# redirect would send the visitor straight back, and the two would loop.
#
# "/" is the home page. Pages does not apply a redirect rule to "/" itself,
# so the root is the one live URL for the home page and every other spelling
# of it is retired to it: /index and /index.html both 301 to the root, which
# is the URL the home page's canonical tag names. "/admin" is left alone:
# the staff console is not part of the public set and has no public twin.

/index              /            301
/index.html         /            301

/menu               /menu.html   301
/menu.html          /menu        200

/soft-play          /soft-play.html  301
/soft-play.html     /soft-play   200

/parties            /parties.html  301
/parties.html       /parties     200

/calendar           /calendar.html  301
/calendar.html      /calendar    200

/contact            /contact.html  301
/contact.html       /contact     200

/privacy            /privacy.html  301
/privacy.html       /privacy     200

/terms              /terms.html  301
/terms.html         /terms       200

/cookies            /cookies.html  301
/cookies.html       /cookies     200

/unsubscribe        /unsubscribe.html  301
/unsubscribe.html   /unsubscribe  200

/404.html           /404         200
